  $$Arjun Raghavan has advised on urban transport and public-private partnerships in India and South Asia for twenty years. He has structured bus concession and metro feeder contracts for state transport undertakings, built financial models for gross-cost and net-cost bus contracts, and prepared electric bus procurement under national incentive schemes. His work also covers energy efficiency in depots and street lighting PPPs. Arjun previously worked in the infrastructure advisory practice of a large accounting firm and has supported the Asian Development Bank and the World Bank on city transport projects in India, Sri Lanka and Bangladesh. He has also worked on value capture around new transit lines and on performance-based payments in bus contracts.$$,
