  $$Sushila Gurung Thapa is a disability inclusion specialist and trainer with eleven years of experience in Nepal. She has trained teachers, local government officials and NGO staff on inclusive education and disability-inclusive programming, and designed training of trainers packages used by organizations of persons with disabilities. She facilitates participatory workshops that bring disabled people's organizations and service providers together, and mentors young disability rights activists. Sushila previously coordinated inclusive primary education pilots in Province 1 and has advised on accessibility standards for school reconstruction after the 2015 earthquake. She also strengthens organisations of persons with disabilities and supports municipalities on disability-inclusive planning.$$,
